@* The wrapper is `relative` because the gradient is `absolute`, and the content is `relative
   z-10` because the gradient sits at -z-10 on purpose. Neither half can come from inside the
   component: it has no idea what it is sitting on. `overflow-hidden` keeps the glow inside the
   panel instead of washing over the page. *@
<div class="relative overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border bg-card px-8 py-12 text-card-foreground">
    <Spotlight />
    <div class="relative z-10 flex max-w-md flex-col gap-3">
        <p class="text-sm font-medium text-muted-foreground">Release 4.2</p>
        <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Everything in one place</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
            A panel with a pool of light behind it. The glow is decoration — the words below are
            the content, and they read exactly the same without it.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>
